use Libraries.Web.Page.QuorumPage

/*
    Lab 6.5: Understanding Focus.
    Converted from the old Lesson page by plan 13's generator: the same
    words, now without Tailwind.
*/
class Lab6_5 is QuorumPage
    // A double quote, for code and words that hold one.
    text dq = ""

    on create
        SetLocation("lessons/chapter6/lab6_5.html")
        // The name lists and links use, and the series and track it belongs
        // to: its section and picture.
        SetShortTitle("Lab 6.5")
        // For search engines and link previews, and what lists of pages say.
        SetSummary("an introduction to using focus.")
    end

    action Setup
        dq = dq:GetDoubleQuote()
        SetWebPageTitle("Lab 6.5: Understand Focus")
        Title("Lab 6.5: Understanding Focus")
        Paragraph("Understanding how common focus systems work")
        Objectives()
        Overview()
        Task1GettingStarted()
        Task2InheritingFromTheFocusObserverClass()
        Task3UsingTheObserverClass()
        SampleOutput()
    end

    private action Objectives
        Section("Objectives")
        Paragraph("The goal of this lab is to understand the following concepts:")
        BulletList()
        ListItem("Using a class hierarchical system")
        ListItem("How to instantiate blueprint actions")
        ListItem("How to use the Libraries.Accessibility classes")
    end

    private action Overview
        Section("Overview")
        Paragraph("In lab 6.4 we built a screen reader that told us what key on the keyboard was pressed. In Quorum, we can write screen readers that do even more. In this lab we will make another screen reader that will tell us when a new window, button, or any other component has gained focus.")
    end

    private action Task1GettingStarted
        Section("Task 1: Getting Started")
        Paragraph("Start Sodbeans. Create a new “Quorum Application” project, and name it Lab6_5. In the Main.quorum file, it should contain a Main class and Main action.")
        Paragraph("We will need to create an additional class in this project. In the New File dialog, create a new file by selecting “Quorum” and “Quorum Class” in the Categories and File Types windows, respectively. Then, name the new file Observer in the New Quorum Class dialog.")
        Paragraph("Don't forget to include the appropriate libraries!")
    end

    private action Task2InheritingFromTheFocusObserverClass
        Section("Task 2: Inheriting from the FocusObserver Class")
        Paragraph("Just like in Lab 6.4, our Observer class will need to inherit the variables and actions of an observer class. The class we need to include in order to get the events that involve the focus changing is the FocusObserver class. Just as in the last lab, use the is keyword to inherit from the FocusObserver class.")
        CodeExample("use Libraries.Accessibility.all 
use Libraries.Sound.Speech

class Observer is FocusObserver
end", "")
        Paragraph("Just as in Lab 6.4, our Observer class is going to need an instance of the Speech class to say things quickly.")
        Paragraph("We will also need to implement the blueprint action ReceiveEvent in our Observer class. In Lab 6.4 we used the GetDescription action to explain the event, but you can also get the individual aspects of the event and make your own sentence to describe the event. The FocusEvent class has quite a few actions that you can use to get individual information about the event.")
        BulletList()
        ListItem("GetCategory(): For FocusEvents this will always be "):DoubleQuote():Text("Focus"):DoubleQuote():Text(".")
        ListItem("GetAction(): This returns a short indication of what was focused (e.g. Desktop, SwitchWindow, MouseCaptureStart).")
        ListItem("GetComponent(): This returns a short description of the type of element that was focused (e.g. Button, Window, MenuItem).")
        ListItem("GetComponentName(): This returns the name of the component that was focused(e.g. Cancel, Sodbeans 3.5, File).")
        ListItem("GetKeyboardShortcut(): This returns the keyboard shortcut of the component that was focused.")
        ListItem("GetChildCount(): This returns the number of children the event has For example, when you focus on a list it will tell you the number of items that list has in it.")
        ListItem("GetChild(integer index): This returns an AccessibleChild representing the child at the index of the parameter, if it is a valid index.")
        Paragraph("Use any or all of these actions to create a description of the event and use the Speech object to say it.")
        CodeExample("action ReceiveEvent(FocusEvent event)
    speech:Say(" + dq + "The " + dq + " + event:GetComponent() + " + dq + ", " + dq + " + event:GetComponentName() + " + dq + ", was focused. Its keyboard shortcut is " + dq + " + event:GetKeyboardShortcut() + " + dq + "." + dq + ")
end", "")
        Paragraph("Above is an example of how you could combine the parts of the event to make a sentence to describe it.")
    end

    private action Task3UsingTheObserverClass
        Section("Task 3: Using the Observer class")
        Paragraph("Now that we have implemented the Observer class, we can add an instance of it to our of AccessibilityManager. You can then start the AccessibilityManager and begin listening for events just as you did in Lab 6.4.")
    end

    private action SampleOutput
        Section("Sample Output")
        Paragraph("When you run the program it should not do anything until you focus on something (open a new window or click a button or menu). Once you do that it should say out loud the sentence you created.")
        Paragraph("When you are done, debug and fix any errors, then show your code to your instructor.")
    end
end
